gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip=Machine Type: §eRemote Multiblock Host§r\nRuns explicitly bound machines of one type from centralized I/O and energy hatches\nRemote machines remain formed and keep energy hatches only to define voltage, amperage and overclocking\nPut the target machine controller item in this controller slot to select its type\nNormal, multi-amp and laser hatches are supported; all capacity becomes one aggregate recipe\nBatch mode is supported; disabling work finishes the current recipe first; progress is shown in seconds\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§eBinding setup:\n§f1. Craft and hold a Hosted Machine Binder\n§f2. Shift-left-click the host controller to record it\n§f3. Right-click a remote controller to add or remove it\n§f4. Drone DownLinks only provide maintenance and never auto-host machines\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidance
gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip_secondary=§fSize: §63§7x§63§7x§63§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure:\n   §fController: §7Front center\n   §616+ §fZPM Machine Casings\n   §eExactly 1 §fMaintenance Hatch (Drone DownLink allowed): §7Any casing\n   §e1 exotic or 1-2 normal §fEnergy Hatches (multi-amp/laser supported): §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus/Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus/Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §fAir: §7Center\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f on the controller to visualize/build it!
